0..68 Comment "//! `task-base` declares the shared protocols for every task source."
69..72 Comment "//!"
73..147 Comment "//! A fork makes the parent and task peers. The task gives its result back"
148..220 Comment "//! on its end. A fork is the parallel product of two strategies, and an"
221..260 Comment "//! operation is a move of one of them."
261..264 Comment "//!"
265..345 Comment "//! The parent reads the end to its close and joins. No task outlives its parent"
346..385 Comment "//! or the Trio nursery that starts it."
386..389 Comment "//!"
390..466 Comment "//! - cites: [Mellies-2020-concurrent_separation_logic_meets_template_games]"
467..651 Comment "//! [Mellies-2020-concurrent_separation_logic_meets_template_games]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3373718.3394762 \"Melliès and Stefanesco, Concurrent Separation Logic Meets Template Games\""
